---
source: crates/vps-ready/src/cli/module_docs.rs
expression: out
---
{
  "id": "net.tunnel",
  "title": "Run a Cloudflare Tunnel connector, for a website with no public port",
  "applies": true,
  "arms_safety_timer": false,
  "why": "A web server on ports 80 and 443 is open to every scanner on the internet. A Cloudflare Tunnel connector opens outbound connections to Cloudflare's edge and receives visitors through them, so the host needs no inbound port at all; firewall.inbound can then leave 80 and 443 closed.",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "provider",
      "default": "\"cloudflare\"",
      "help": "The tunnel provider; \"cloudflare\" is the only one."
    },
    {
      "name": "token_file",
      "default": "\"\"",
      "help": "A file holding the token of a tunnel created in the Cloudflare dashboard, owned by root with mode 0600, not a symlink, in directories only root can write to. The connector's unit copies it at each start (`LoadCredential=`); the module never reads it (the guided setup only checks whether an existing file holds a token). After replacing it, run `sudo systemctl restart vps-ready-cloudflared`. Empty: cloudflared is installed, and no connector runs."
    },
    {
      "name": "auto_update",
      "default": "true",
      "help": "Let unattended-upgrades (updates.auto) install cloudflared's updates; a path unit then restarts the connector on the new binary, which drops visitors' connections for a moment."
    }
  ],
  "controls": []
}
